Z||000000||MooCow||08-12-2000||05:51 PM||||Well the engine in my car is pretty good but has 131,000 or so on it and it still has the origanal clutch on it!  So I really want to do a 3.8 super chared engine but will not have enough money next year so i am going to wait until I have enough.  So should I just buy the 3.4 from a camaro and do that conversion for around 1000 and at that timne change it to the auto casue I dont want a 4 speed anymore.  then keep the 3.4 engine for 2 summers then have enough for a paint job and the new engine.  Think I should do that? I really dont think my clutch will last one more summer cause it always grinds when I take off at times in 1st and when I take of in 2nd sometimes it grinds. It also does it in reverse at times. It sounds like metal scratching the ground when it does that.<BR>So is this agood idea or just a waste of money????    All input will help.<P><BR>                             Thanks Ken<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||mbramble||08-12-2000||07:20 PM||||I'd say, since you say your current engine is running well, just go and have the clutch replaced.  I just had a new one put in my '91 S-10 for $400 at a local transmiision shop.  I shopped around to compare prices between the national shops (AAMCO) and the Chevy dealers and they beat both them in price and have the same warranty.  <P>If your current engine is good, why do a conversion now and then do another one in the future?? Now that seems like a waste of money to me.  Have the clutch repaired and save the money you would spend on the interim conversion and you should be able to do the converion you really want sooner.<P>My 2 cents.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||08-12-2000||07:50 PM||||Grinding into gears?  Maybe you're clutch hydraulics aren't up to snuff.  But is the clutch slipping at all?||||reg||1
Z||000003||MooCow||08-12-2000||11:53 PM||||No the clutch isn't slipping at all.  I can barley push it in and it will grip very nicley.  I have reved this car up to 5 grand in every gear and it grips everytime I do it.  It's just on some days it makes a grinding noise only when I go from a stop then go.  The lady I bought it from never brought the car ever past 3 grand cause she shiftedwhen it said shift everytime.  I even have every record since 1986 on this car.<BR>All I know is that I really want an automatic. I am sick of shifting. I just want to be able to hit the gas and go.<P>                                Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||08-13-2000||01:13 PM||||if the engine runs good then check the pressure on all cyinders and see where they are at, if it's in within the specs why pay when your motor is good, now if it comes out bad then do it other wise i would fix the clutch and save more money for when it does go out. <B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||08-13-2000||02:02 PM||||Mine did that sometimes. It was the flywheel dust cover  rubbing on the flywheel, the pressure plate was putting enough force on the flywheel that it rubbed a little bit. It could also be a bad torque strut making the motor and transaxle move enough to rub on something.<P>If you want an auto, get the 4spd off a newer car since that will go nicely with the 3.8 when you get it.||||reg||1
